Psiphon-Labs/quic-go: build http3 against quic-go/qpack v0.6

Psiphon's quic-go fork calls the qpack v0.4 decoder: NewDecoder takes a
callback and the Decoder has DecodeFull. Xray-core needs qpack v0.6.0, where
NewDecoder takes no argument and DecodeFull is gone. One Go build holds one
version of a module, so without this patch the fork's http3 package does not
compile next to Xray-core.

The patch changes only those calls. The new http3/qpack_compat.go adds
decodeFull, which does what v0.4's DecodeFull did, using v0.6's Decode. The
encoder API is the same in both versions. Inside psiphon-tunnel-core this
code runs only for meek over QUIC (psiphon/common/quic/quic.go, the
http3.RoundTripper that psiphon/meekConn.go uses).

Base:    github.com/Psiphon-Labs/quic-go v0.0.0-20250527153145-79fe45fb83b1
         (commit 79fe45fb83b1), the version psiphon-tunnel-core v2.0.41
         (commit 96f782c6f662) requires.
Source:  written for Fortiva.
Licence: MIT, the same as quic-go and Psiphon's fork of it.

  http3/client.go        NewDecoder() without the callback
  http3/conn.go          NewDecoder() without the callback, one decodeFull
  http3/http_stream.go   one decodeFull
  http3/server.go        one decodeFull
  http3/qpack_compat.go  decodeFull (new file)

The fork's own http3 tests still use the v0.4 API and do not compile, so
the test for this patch lives outside the fork, in android/core/psiphonquic/:
one HTTP/3 request on 127.0.0.1 that goes through every changed call.

Apply with: patch -p1 < qpack-v0.6.patch   (stage-psiphon.sh does this)

